add('Economy','01 · National accounts','Q2 GDP: real growth, sector mix and release vintage','November’s release covered July–September 2025.','Real GDP grew 8.2% year-on-year at constant 2011–12 prices.|Real GVA growth was 8.1%.|Financial/real-estate/professional services grew 10.2%; manufacturing 9.1%.','GDP at market prices differs from sectoral GVA; constant-price growth differs from nominal growth.','Examine the base, sector contributions and jobs rather than one headline.|Preserve this historical base-year/release vintage; later statistical rebasing or revisions must not silently rewrite it.','This is a quarterly outturn estimate, not full-year growth, a December forecast, or proof every sector grew 8.2%.','How should strong GDP growth be evaluated for quality and inclusion?')
add('Economy','02 · Standards and trade','Quality Control Orders: targeted withdrawals, not no standards','Several ministries withdrew or suspended specified orders.','The changes cover selected electrical, metal, steel and chemical products.|Some measures defer enforcement while others rescind orders.|Already implemented electrical orders have specified exceptions.','Mandatory conformity requirements and the underlying existence of a technical standard are distinct.','Input-cost relief should be balanced with safety and testing capacity.|Read the product-specific notification before claiming an industry-wide exemption.','Do not say every QCO or every BIS standard was abolished nationwide.','How can standards policy avoid both unsafe imports and disproportionate compliance costs?')
add('Society & Welfare','01 · Labour legal transition','Four Labour Codes: effective date versus operational detail','The government made the Codes effective from 21 November.','Wages, Industrial Relations, Social Security and OSHWC are the four Codes.|They consolidate 29 central labour laws.|Central/state rules, schemes and transition arrangements remain important.','Enactment, commencement and operational implementation are separate stages; delegated rules fill statutory detail.','Connect September drafts and October consultations to this commencement milestone.|Do not convert a broad official benefit description into proof every worker had received every scheme benefit.','Neither “only a draft in November” nor “all detailed rules and benefits fully operational everywhere” is accurate.','How can labour-law consolidation improve protection without widening implementation gaps?',True,src=['E7-LABOUR','E7-PRS11'],day=21)
add('Society & Welfare','02 · EPF regularisation','Employees’ Enrolment Scheme: conditional past-period relief','A special EPF window opened on 1 November.','Eligible past non-enrolment covers July 2017–October 2025.|The window runs to 30 April 2026.|Employee-share relief does not waive the employer’s share, interest and administrative charges; specified damages are ₹100.','Regularisation differs from cancellation of all liabilities or compulsory new benefits for unrelated workers.','Accessible enrolment and credible records can expand coverage.|Safeguards should prevent employers using amnesty to normalise repeated non-compliance.','Do not call ₹100 the total employer liability or extend the relief automatically outside the covered period.','How can compliance amnesties expand social protection without rewarding evasion?',True)
add('Security','01 · Industrial hazard prevention','Draft oil-mine safety rules: site-specific risk management','The ministry invited comments under the OSHWC Code.','Owners must prepare safety-management and emergency-response plans in the proposal.|Blowouts, toxic gas and hazardous operations require specific controls.|Untreated-fluid discharge and continuous gas detection are addressed.','A generic compliance checklist cannot substitute for a site-specific hazard assessment.','Contractor competence and maintenance integrity matter alongside owner duties.|AP’s hydrocarbon context makes emergency coordination and environmental safeguards relevant.','The draft is not proof every site already complied or that every proposed rule had final force.','What makes high-hazard industry regulation preventive rather than reactive?',True)
add('Polity & Governance','01 · Data protection phases','DPDP Rules: notification does not activate everything at once','The 2025 Rules were notified in November.','Board-related rules have immediate effect in the reviewed account.|Core processing obligations are phased to eighteen months after publication.|Notices must explain data, purpose and withdrawal mechanisms.','A notified rulebook can have staggered commencement; institutional establishment and enforceable processing duties differ.','Map January consultation to November notification without assuming every draft clause survived.|Organisations need inventories, workable consent flows and breach-response systems before deadlines.','Do not say every processing duty began on notification day or every provision was deferred equally.','How should phased privacy implementation produce real user control rather than paperwork?')
add('Polity & Governance','02 · Children and consent','Children’s data: verifiable consent with purpose-specific exceptions','The notified privacy rules describe parental verification.','Verification may use reliable identity information or authorised digital tokens.|The parent must be an adult.|Healthcare, education and childcare exceptions are limited to specified purposes.','Age assurance and data minimisation must work together; collecting more identity data creates risks of its own.','Design accessible alternatives and minimise repeated sensitive-data collection.|An institutional exception should not become unrestricted commercial use of children’s data.','Do not treat every education-related data use as exempt or a token as permission for any later purpose.','How can child-data safeguards avoid exclusion and excessive surveillance?')
add('Economy','03 · Export ecosystem','Export Promotion Mission: finance plus market readiness','The Cabinet approved the Budget-announced mission on 12 November.','The outlay is ₹25,060 crore for FY2025–26 to FY2030–31.|Niryat Protsahan addresses affordable trade finance.|Niryat Disha addresses non-financial readiness; DGFT is the implementing agency.','Credit constraints, standards compliance and logistics are different bottlenecks requiring complementary interventions.','AP marine/MSME exporters need both finance and credible quality/traceability.|Use the fiscal-year range rather than copy the review’s inconsistent “five years” shorthand.','An approved envelope is not money already paid; do not reverse the two sub-schemes.','What would make export support effective for first-time and interior-district exporters?',True,src=['E7-EPM','E7-PRS11'],day=12)
add('Science & Technology','01 · Strategic materials','Rare-earth magnets: oxide-to-magnet capacity target','The Cabinet approved the sintered REPM scheme on 26 November.','The scheme outlay is ₹7,280 crore.|It targets 6,000 tonnes per annum of integrated capacity.|Duration is seven years from award: two-year gestation plus five years of sales-linked support.','Reserves, separated oxides, metals, alloys and finished magnets are different supply-chain capabilities.','Competitive selection and reliable inputs must accompany capital support.|Do not add announced scheme support components into an invented arithmetic breakdown of the total.','6,000 MTPA is planned annual capacity, not output already produced or a measure of mineral reserves.','How can India reduce strategic-material dependence beyond mining alone?',src=['E7-MAGNET','E7-PRS11'],day=26)
add('Culture & History','01 · GI authenticity','Draft GI-logo guidelines: traceability over generic branding','DPIIT sought comments on use of the logo.','Misleading use and products failing specified standards are addressed.|The draft excludes logo use on processed products merely using GI goods as inputs.|Registration, authorised use and product compliance remain distinct.','A GI links origin with a quality or reputation; it is not a generic quality mark for any producer.','AP craft/food value chains need authentic producer access and enforcement.|Check final guidelines before treating the consultation as settled operational law.','Using a GI ingredient does not automatically entitle a processed product to use the GI logo.','How can GI protection improve producer value without misleading consumers?',True,p='P2')
add('International Relations','01 · Negotiation milestones','Israel FTA terms: not the September investment treaty','Terms of reference were signed to begin FTA negotiations.','They define the negotiation’s scope and procedure.|Goods/services access and investment are intended areas.|This is distinct from September’s bilateral investment agreement.','Negotiation launch, conclusion, signature and entry into force have different legal consequences.','Predictability can benefit trade but depends on final schedules and origin rules.|Do not collapse two separate instruments into one completed trade pact.','Terms of reference do not prove tariffs were already eliminated.','How should trade and investment agreements complement one another?',p='P2')
add('Economy','04 · Export credit relief','RBI trade relief: time extension is not debt cancellation','RBI announced foreign-exchange and credit measures.','Export-proceeds realisation/repatriation was extended from nine to fifteen months.|Specified advance-payment shipment periods were extended.|Conditional moratorium relief covered eligible non-defaulting exporters with outstanding facilities at 31 August.','A moratorium postpones payments; it does not automatically extinguish principal or interest.','Cash-flow relief helps viable exporters survive external shocks.|AP fish/textile exporters must check commodity, facility and date conditions, not assume universal eligibility.','Do not call the measures an unconditional loan waiver or apply the covered dates to every borrower.','How can temporary export relief preserve viability without hiding credit risk?',True)
add('Polity & Governance','03 · Assent reference','Presidential reference: no court-made universal assent clock','The Court delivered its advisory opinion on 20 November.','The reference concerned Articles 200/201 and assent to state Bills.|The opinion rejects judicially prescribed timelines and deemed assent.|Limited directions remain possible for prolonged inaction.','Article 143 advisory jurisdiction differs from ordinary merits adjudication; operative reasoning matters.','Link April’s ruling, May’s reference and November’s opinion as a developing constitutional debate.|Do not extrapolate limited non-justiciability into complete immunity for indefinite inactivity.','Do not repeat April’s timeline propositions as an unchanged November position or say every delay is beyond all scrutiny.','How can constitutional restraint coexist with accountability for prolonged inaction?')
add('Polity & Governance','04 · Tribunal independence','Tribunal reform: invalidated provisions and a commission direction','The Court struck down specified 2021 Act provisions.','The challenged areas included eligibility, appointments and tenure.|The Court linked these provisions to judicial independence.|It directed a National Tribunals Commission within four months.','Appointment design affects independence; a direction to establish a body is not proof the body exists.','Executive accountability must not become control over adjudication.|Track compliance and later orders independently rather than assume the deadline was met.','Do not say all tribunals were abolished or the commission was operational immediately.','What institutional safeguards make tribunals credible alternatives to courts?')
add('Environment','01 · Environmental-clearance review','Retrospective EC: November review changes May’s position','A review ruling recalled the earlier prohibition.','Exceptional retrospective clearance was recognised in the reviewed account.|The 2017 notification’s application is limited to violations existing on 14 March 2017.|Prior EC remains a distinct baseline requirement.','Exceptional regularisation is not a prospective licence to violate environmental law.','Read the review with the earlier May note; retain dated positions instead of silently presenting both as current.|Compensation, appraisal and deterrence remain separate policy concerns.','Do not call every future violation regularisable or omit the notification’s cut-off date.','How can environmental law address legacy violations without encouraging new ones?')
add('Agriculture','01 · Seed regulation','Draft Seeds Bill: quality registration with exceptions','The ministry invited comments on replacement of the 1966 Act.','Sale of seed varieties generally requires registration in the draft.|Farmers’ varieties and export-only varieties have specified exceptions.|State registration, traceability and a central portal/QR mechanism feature.','Seed quality regulation and plant-variety intellectual-property protection are separate regimes.','Traceability can deter spurious seeds when inspection, testing and accessible remedies work.|AP farmers need affordable reliable seed and functioning complaint mechanisms.','The draft is not an enacted replacement or a ban on every traditional seed exchange.','How can seed regulation protect farmers while encouraging innovation?',True)
add('Economy','05 · Specialty steel','Specialty-steel PLI: third-round conditions','The ministry launched another application round.','The review describes twenty-two product subcategories.|Eligible Indian companies must undertake end-to-end manufacturing.|Sales-linked incentives vary by category and require verified performance.','New rounds, revised eligibility and realised incremental production are not interchangeable.','Specialised grades can matter for defence/power supply chains.|Do not add every round’s headline as fresh independent money without checking the overall scheme envelope.','A capacity target is not commissioned production or a guaranteed incentive to every applicant.','How should industrial incentives demonstrate technology and production additionality?',p='P2')
add('Security','02 · Defence R&D cooperation','DRDO–France DGA: cooperation framework, not automatic transfer','The agencies signed an R&D collaboration agreement.','Joint research, training and testing are included.|Platforms, unmanned systems, cyber and sensors are potential areas.|Information/equipment/know-how exchanges sit within the framework.','A cooperation instrument differs from delivery of a particular weapon or unrestricted technology ownership.','Local absorption needs skilled teams, manufacturing capability and workable IP arrangements.|Project-specific evidence is needed before asserting successful indigenisation.','Do not call an R&D framework a completed procurement or unlimited transfer of all French technology.','What enables defence cooperation to build durable indigenous capability?',p='P2')
add('Environment','02 · Thermal co-firing','Revised co-firing policy: differentiated regional blends','The power ministry revised biomass co-firing policy.','Eligible fuel now includes MSW-based torrefied charcoal.|NCR plants face 5% biomass plus an additional 2% specified blend.|Outside NCR the mandate is at least 5% of specified eligible fuel by weight.','Torrefaction uses low-oxygen heating; co-firing mixes fuels rather than making coal renewable.','Reliable feedstock and pollution safeguards determine practical benefits.|NCR-specific residue sourcing should not be presented as an identical nationwide condition.','Do not generalise the NCR blend to every plant or assume mixed-fuel combustion is emission-free.','How can co-firing policy connect residue management with credible power-sector safeguards?',True)
add('Polity & Governance','05 · Access to justice','Legal aid: thirty years of implementation, not enactment','The issue marked the Act’s November 1995 implementation.','The Legal Services Authorities Act was enacted in 1987.|Article 39A links legal aid with equal justice.|National, state and district institutions support access.','Statutory eligibility includes categories as well as prescribed income conditions; income is not the only route.','Competent representation and early help matter beyond assigning a lawyer.|Do not reproduce undated income ceilings or conflate patron-in-chief and executive-chair roles.','1995 commencement does not mean the Act was enacted in 1995 or aid is only for convicted prisoners.','How should legal aid be measured by effective access rather than appointments?',True,slug='legal-aid-in-india')
add('International Relations','02 · G20 and the Global South','Johannesburg G20: African venue and voluntary cooperation','The issue reviewed the first G20 summit on African soil.','The theme was solidarity, equality and sustainability.|Debt, resilience, energy and development featured.|The critical-minerals framework is voluntary and non-binding.','G20 political coordination does not create a supranational legislature or automatic domestic law.','Assess follow-through and financing, not declarations alone.|AU participation helps representation but does not eliminate differences among African economies.','Do not treat every target as binding or a political declaration as proof of delivered electrification.','How can the G20 improve the voice and practical policy space of developing economies?',slug='g20')
add('Environment','03 · COP30 outcomes','Belém: implementation tools and unresolved fossil-fuel language','COP30 met in Brazil; UNU analyses the negotiated outcomes.','The package includes adaptation indicators and implementation initiatives.|Tripling adaptation finance by 2035 is a political signal, not money already delivered.|Formal fossil-fuel phase-out language did not land in the outcome described.','Mitigation, adaptation and just-transition support address different needs.','Distinguish negotiated decisions, presidency initiatives and actual disbursements.|AP coastal resilience links global finance debates to local vulnerability without assuming direct allocations.','Do not call a presidency roadmap a universally negotiated phase-out or a finance signal a binding paid commitment.','What does COP30 reveal about implementation gains and ambition gaps?',True,src=['E7-COP'],slug='unfccc-cop-30')
add('Science & Technology','02 · One Health systems','One Health: integrated surveillance beyond human hospitals','The magazine discussed the mission and preparedness architecture.','The approach links human, animal and environmental health.|Coordinated surveillance, diagnostics and outbreak response are central.|Research tools and community participation support readiness.','Zoonotic threats cross administrative sectors; data integration requires compatible standards and lawful sharing.','AP livestock, aquaculture and public-health systems provide practical convergence settings.|The magazine’s future-launch wording does not establish that One Health originated in November.','Do not date every approval, institution and launch to the coverage month or equate One Health with only zoonoses.','How can inter-sectoral surveillance improve preparedness without fragmenting accountability?',True,slug='national-one-health-mission-nohm')
add('Society & Welfare','03 · Antimicrobial stewardship','NAP-AMR 2.0: a multisectoral 2025–29 plan','The health minister launched the updated action plan.','The magazine identifies the 2025–29 horizon.|It emphasises One Health, surveillance and stewardship.|Time-bound sector actions and environmental monitoring feature.','Resistance develops in microorganisms, not because a human body becomes immune to an antibiotic.','Prescription audits and diagnostics must coexist with access to necessary treatment.|Plan approval is not evidence resistance fell or all departmental budgets were spent.','Do not equate AMR solely with antibiotic use in human hospitals or recommend denial of appropriate therapy.','How can stewardship address misuse while preserving equitable access?',True,slug='national-action-plan-on-antimicrobial-resistance-20')
add('Culture & History','02 · Tribal resistance','Birsa Munda at 150: land, dignity and Ulgulan','The issue marked his 1875 birth and Janjatiya Gaurav Divas.','Birsa belonged to the Munda community of Chhotanagpur.|Ulgulan challenged colonial and exploitative agrarian relations.|15 November is observed as Janjatiya Gaurav Divas.','Tribal resistance involved political, economic and cultural claims rather than a single undifferentiated cause.','Link historical land alienation to contemporary safeguards without implying all tribal movements were identical.|Avoid an oversimplified claim that one 1793 enactment alone directly abolished every local land institution.','Do not confuse a birth anniversary with the year of the uprising or relocate him to an AP tribe.','How did tribal resistance combine identity, land rights and anti-colonial politics?',slug='bhagwan-birsa-munda',p='P2')
add('Society & Welfare','04 · GS4 neuroethics','Neurotechnology: mental privacy and meaningful agency','The issue considered brain–computer interfaces and ethics.','Systems interpret neural signals for device interaction.|Therapeutic uses include communication and prosthetic control.|Risks include inference, data monetisation, coercion and unequal access.','Decoding a limited task signal is not infallible unrestricted reading of every private thought.','Consent must address sensitive data, updates and withdrawal possibilities.|Distinguish demonstrated clinical results from broad consumer or surveillance claims.','Do not call every neural inference accurate or assume ordinary app consent is sufficient for all invasive uses.','What safeguards preserve cognitive liberty while enabling therapeutic innovation?',slug='ethics-of-neuro-tech-revolution',p='P2')
add('Agriculture','02 · Breeders and farmers','PPV&FR: seed rights are not unrestricted branded-seed sales','The issue revisited the 2001 sui generis framework.','It recognises breeders’, researchers’ and farmers’ interests.|Farmers can conserve/use/exchange seed subject to statutory limits.|Selling branded seed of a protected variety is treated differently.','Sui generis protection differs from granting patents over every plant; seed-quality law is another layer.','Innovation incentives should coexist with conservation and farmer access.|Do not infer UPOV membership or repeat the doubtful “silver jubilee” label from 2001 to 2025.','Farmer seed rights do not mean unrestricted commercial branded sales of every protected variety.','How should plant-variety protection balance breeding innovation and farmers’ rights?',True,slug='protection-of-plant-varieties-and-farmers-rights-act-2001')
add('Andhra Pradesh','01 · Investment pipeline','CII Vizag summit: MoUs are proposed investment','The 14–15 November summit produced reported commitments.','TNIE reports 613 MoUs worth about ₹13.25 lakh crore.|The reported 16.31 lakh jobs are expected from proposals.|Government follow-up and regional spread were stated priorities.','MoU value, financial closure, construction, commissioned assets and net employment are different indicators.','Track implementation milestones, cancellations and overlap with earlier announcements.|Do not add the Google hub again as unrelated fresh spending if already included in an aggregate pipeline.','Headlines saying investment “attracted” do not prove the full amount was already spent or jobs created.','How should AP turn investment commitments into verified inclusive development?',True,src=['E7-SUMMIT'],day=15)
add('Andhra Pradesh','02 · MSME geography','AP’s constituency MSME-park plan: announced, not all built','The summit account described decentralised growth intentions.','The CM announced MSME parks across 175 Assembly constituencies.|Common infrastructure and entrepreneurship support were envisaged.|Regional industry, horticulture and aquaculture roles were described.','A spatial target is not evidence of serviced land, occupancy or viable enterprises at every site.','Evaluate power, logistics, credit, market links and local skills before site-count success claims.|Rayalaseema’s district-specific water and value-chain constraints require evidence beyond broad regional slogans.','Do not describe all 175 parks as operational or promise identical industries/jobs to every constituency.','What determines whether dispersed industrial parks create durable local livelihoods?',True,src=['E7-SUMMIT'])
add('Polity & Governance','06 · Parliamentary scrutiny','Committee work programme: agenda is not a finding','PRS lists issues selected for future examination.','Education, health, rail safety and defence modernisation appear on the agenda.|Selected subjects identify intended scrutiny.|Reports, recommendations and government action come later.','Agenda-setting, evidence-taking, report adoption and implementation are separate oversight stages.','Use the list to identify research gaps rather than cite unissued conclusions.|A work programme cannot establish an audit failure or a reform already accepted.','Do not turn “to examine” into “committee found” or “government implemented”.','How can parliamentary scrutiny strengthen evidence-based executive accountability?',p='P2')
m='2025-12'
add('Economy','01 · Monetary policy','December MPC: 25-basis-point cut with neutral stance','The December decision moved repo to 5.25%.','Repo fell from 5.5% to 5.25%.|SDF became 5%; MSF/bank rate became 5.5%.|FY2025–26 growth was projected at 7.3%, up from 6.8%.','A forecast revision is not a statistical outturn; rate and stance convey different information.','Follow February, April, June, August and October before this next step.|Transmission to actual loan rates depends on benchmarks, repricing and credit conditions.','Do not describe a 0.25 percentage-point move as a 25% cut or 7.3% as measured annual GDP growth.','Why can rate easing coexist with a neutral stance?')
add('Economy','02 · External accounts','Q2 current account: revised Q1 comparator matters','The review reports the July–September balance.','The deficit was USD 12.3 billion, 1.3% of GDP.|The year-earlier deficit was USD 20.9 billion, 2.2%.|The later Q1 comparator is USD 2.7 billion, 0.3%, versus September’s initial USD 2.4 billion, 0.2%.','Revision vintage, reference quarter and publication month must be recorded separately.','Net services and transfers can cushion a goods deficit.|Keep the September note as a historical release, explicitly cross-linked to this later revision rather than silently overwriting it.','A lower year-on-year Q2 deficit does not mean no goods deficit or that the initial Q1 estimate was the final figure.','How should external-account resilience be assessed across statistical revisions?')
add('Economy','03 · Industrial output','IIP Q2: weighted production index, not GDP','Industrial production grew 4.3% in July–September.','Manufacturing output grew 5.1%.|Electricity grew 3.7%; mining declined 0.5%.|Manufacturing has roughly 78% weight in the reviewed index.','IIP measures production volume in covered industries; GDP/GVA are value-added concepts.','Sector weights mean an aggregate need not mirror the weakest or strongest component.|Compare survey period and revision status before linking monthly news with quarterly output.','Do not call IIP growth GDP growth or infer every industrial sector expanded.','What does industrial production reveal that a headline GDP figure may conceal?')
add('Polity & Governance','01 · Statistical institutions','NSC review: statutory autonomy recommended, not granted','The Finance Committee reviewed the statistical system.','It recommended autonomous status with full statutory backing for NSC.|Common standards and a statistical audit function were proposed.|Unorganised-sector measurement was identified as a concern.','A parliamentary recommendation differs from an enacted change in institutional powers.','Transparent methods and revisions support trust more than suppressing inconvenient estimates.|Separate NSC oversight from September’s proposed ISI institutional legislation.','Do not say the report itself enacted a new NSC law or replaced every statistical agency.','What institutional reforms would strengthen official-statistics credibility?')
add('Science & Technology','01 · Nuclear legislation','SHANTI Bill passed: participation, liability and regulation','Parliament passed the nuclear-framework Bill in December.','It provides for licences to specified Indian private entities.|Operator-liability tiers range from ₹100 crore to ₹3,000 crore by capacity.|It grants statutory recognition to AERB.','Legislative passage, assent, commencement, licensing and plant commissioning are distinct milestones.','Investment mobilisation needs independent safety capacity and transparent compensation arrangements.|This note records the reviewed passage-stage framework, not verification of every later operative rule.','Do not describe unrestricted foreign operation or new private plants already commissioned from passage alone.','How can nuclear expansion reconcile investment, safety and compensation?')
add('Science & Technology','02 · Nuclear liability design','Nuclear recourse: supplier grounds and victim compensation differ','The passed framework alters operator recourse.','The prior law included defective equipment/materials as a recourse ground.|The Bill removes that specified ground.|Contractual recourse and deliberate-damage grounds remain relevant in the reviewed account.','Operator liability to victims and recovery from a supplier are different legal relationships.','Assess incentives for quality, insurability and speed of compensation separately.|Removing one statutory ground is not proof every contract-based or other legal remedy disappears.','Do not call the change an abolition of all operator liability or all possible supplier responsibility.','What liability design balances victim protection and credible supplier incentives?')
add('Economy','04 · Hydrocarbon rules','Petroleum Rules 2025: unified lease and environmental duties','New rules replaced the 1959 framework.','State grants concern onshore resources; Centre grants concern offshore resources.|A petroleum lease combines exploration/development/production rights.|Emissions monitoring/reduction and authorised geological storage feature.','A petroleum lease does not itself substitute for every environmental or safety approval.','Shared infrastructure can lower costs but needs liability and access arrangements.|AP’s onshore/offshore interests require the correct jurisdiction and project-level permissions.','Do not generalise offshore authority to state governments or call carbon storage automatically authorised everywhere.','How can upstream reform improve investment while preserving environmental accountability?',True)
add('Environment','01 · Virtual renewable contracts','VPPA: financial settlement, not physical delivery between parties','CERC notified guidelines for virtual power purchase agreements.','The agreement is between a renewable generator and designated consumer.|Earmarked-capacity RECs transfer under the framework.|Contracts last at least one year and are non-tradeable/non-transferable.','A VPPA financially settles price differences while electricity is sold through permitted routes; it is not a private wire supply.','Track renewable attributes to avoid double counting claims.|The bilateral price does not make exposure disappear; contract allocation and settlement matter.','Do not say the two parties physically exchange the contracted electricity or can freely trade the VPPA.','How can financial renewable contracts improve compliance without weakening credibility?',True)
add('Environment','02 · Solar ecosystem scrutiny','Solar review: upstream manufacturing and storage gaps','The Energy Committee evaluated solar projects.','It recommended storage R&D support.|Dedicated support for polysilicon, ingots and wafers was proposed.|Land/right-of-way coordination and scheme acceleration were highlighted.','Module assembly, upstream manufacturing and reliable delivered energy are distinct capabilities.','Installed capacity alone does not show domestic value addition or round-the-clock supply.|Committee suggestions need later government decisions, budgets and implementation checks.','Do not treat a proposed PLI expansion as already notified or every nameplate MW as constant output.','What complements solar-capacity addition in a resilient domestic ecosystem?')
add('Society & Welfare','01 · Electricity delivery audit','Rural electrification audit: connection versus service quality','CAG reviewed DDUGJY and SAUBHAGYA.','It identified gaps in field surveys and project planning.|Actual expenditure differed from sanctioned amounts.|Inspection delays and quality-assurance weaknesses featured.','Sanctioned expenditure, expenditure incurred, connections and reliable electricity service are separate measures.','Verify beneficiary lists before funding and inspect defects through closure.|Do not turn audit-period outputs into a count of all presently unelectrified households.','A connection count does not guarantee reliable, affordable supply or certify all legacy targets were met.','How should electrification success be audited beyond infrastructure counts?',True)
add('Society & Welfare','02 · Rural employment guarantee','VB–G RAM G: household guarantee and fiscal redesign','Parliament passed the replacement rural-employment framework.','The guarantee increases from 100 to 125 days per rural household.|The reviewed ordinary-state funding ratio is 60:40; specified special states use 90:10.|States bear expenditure beyond the Centre’s normative allocation.','A household guarantee is not an individual guaranteed salary; law, budgets, work demand and actual payments differ.','Compare expanded days with state fiscal exposure and enforceability.|AP analysis should assess wage-payment capacity and demand responsiveness, not only the additional 25 days.','Do not say 125 days were automatically worked/paid by every rural person immediately upon passage.','How should an employment guarantee combine entitlement, fiscal sharing and timely delivery?',True)
add('Society & Welfare','03 · Rural work design','Rural employment: seasonal pause and digital safeguards','The new framework includes scheduling and monitoring provisions.','A state may pause programme work for up to sixty days during peak agricultural seasons.|The fifteen-day work-or-unemployment-allowance principle is retained in the review.|Biometric/geospatial/app-based monitoring features.','A seasonal pause differs from reducing the annual entitlement by precisely sixty days in every case.','Scheduling should reflect local labour needs and protect vulnerable households.|Digital monitoring needs correction channels and alternatives when authentication fails.','Do not assume a mandatory identical nationwide pause or that technology eliminates payment exclusion.','How can employment programmes support agriculture without weakening workers’ fallback security?',True)
add('Polity & Governance','02 · Land acquisition safeguards','LARR implementation report: consent and service-ready rehabilitation','The committee examined the 2013 Act’s implementation.','It noted Gram Sabha consultation/consent being reduced to formality.|It recommended broader mandatory Gram Sabha involvement.|It sought functional rehabilitation sites before possession and alignment with PESA/FRA.','The report’s recommendations must not be presented as fresh amendments already enacted.','Meaningful participation requires understandable information and real rehabilitation readiness.|AP irrigation/industrial projects need project-specific rights and acquisition-stage checks.','Do not convert a committee proposal for all acquisitions into an existing universal statutory rule.','How can acquisition deliver public infrastructure without hollowing out community safeguards?',True)
add('Economy','05 · Insurance reform','Insurance Bill: 100% FDI ceiling is not universal insurance','Parliament passed amendments to insurance laws.','The framework raises the foreign-equity ceiling from 74% to 100%.|Foreign reinsurer net-owned-fund requirements fall from ₹5,000 crore to ₹1,000 crore.|IRDAI receives additional oversight powers.','Foreign ownership permission, capital inflows, product availability and effective household coverage differ.','Competition needs sound solvency and accessible claims/complaint systems.|Keep September’s individual-policy GST relief and AP hybrid cover proposals legally distinct.','Do not say every insurer became foreign-owned or every household automatically insured.','How can insurance liberalisation deepen protection rather than ownership change alone?',True)
add('Economy','06 · Securities Code proposal','Securities Markets Code: introduced and referred, not enacted','The Bill seeks to consolidate three central statutes.','It covers securities contracts, SEBI and depositories.|Registration of intermediaries/market infrastructure remains central.|It adds conflict-of-interest and grievance-redress proposals.','Consolidation can simplify a framework without resolving every regulatory-capacity problem.','Clear recusal standards and accessible redress matter alongside structural changes.|Track committee scrutiny and final text instead of backdating enactment to introduction.','Do not claim the three Acts had already been repealed merely because the Code was introduced.','How should market-law consolidation protect investors and regulatory independence?')
add('Economy','07 · Demerit taxation','Tobacco excise and pan-masala cess: separate instruments','Parliament passed two relevant tax Bills.','One increases central excise on specified tobacco categories.|Another creates a production-based pan-masala cess.|The cess uses machine/unit parameters rather than being simply the GST rate.','Excise, cess and GST have different legal bases and implementation instruments.','Follow September’s deferred tobacco transition rather than claim an identical rate began then.|Check commencement and product-specific notifications for actual liability.','Do not add headline percentages mechanically or backdate December legislation to all September supplies.','How can demerit taxation balance health objectives, compliance and fiscal transition?')
add('Economy','08 · IBC scrutiny','IBC Select Committee: conflict management in liquidation','The committee reported on the August amendment Bill.','It recommended separating the resolution professional from the liquidator role.|It sought clearer CoC supervision boundaries.|It proposed lowering specified creditor initiation thresholds from 66% to 51%.','A committee recommendation is not an operative amendment; creditor roles and statutory adjudication differ.','Assess incentives to prefer liquidation for additional fees and guard commercial wisdom with due process.|Avoid mixing this Select Committee with the separate general IBC performance report.','Do not apply the suggested 51% threshold as already binding solely on this report.','How should insolvency reform align professional incentives with value preservation?')
add('Society & Welfare','04 · Higher education Bill','VBSA: regulatory consolidation without grant allocation','The Bill was introduced and referred to a Joint Committee.','It proposes replacing UGC, AICTE and NCTE.|Separate councils cover regulation, accreditation and standards.|The apex body/councils do not receive institutional grant-allocation powers in the proposal.','Regulatory power and funding authority are different institutional tools.','Assess autonomy, accountability and coordination between funders/regulators.|Introduction does not prove existing statutory bodies had already ceased operating.','Do not call the Bill enacted or assume every UGC function transfers unchanged to one new body.','How can higher-education regulation improve quality while protecting institutional autonomy?')
add('Society & Welfare','05 · Education access review','Education-loan review: recommendations are not entitlements','The committee examined financial access to higher education.','It recommended improved collateral-free access and repayment moratorium arrangements.|It proposed broader institutional coverage and relief from credit-score barriers for specified families.|The PM Vidyalakshmi framework still has eligibility conditions.','Loan sanction, interest subsidy, collateral rules and repayment moratorium are separate benefits.','Assess information access, processing delay and graduate earnings risk.|Do not turn a proposed two-year moratorium into a universal already-operative bank rule.','An education-loan committee report does not automatically waive debt or guarantee admission/funding.','How can higher-education finance widen opportunity without unmanageable debt?',True)
add('International Relations','01 · Russia ties','India–Russia summit: agreements and implementation','The Russian President visited India for bilateral talks.','Cooperation covers nuclear, space, defence and maritime fields.|A urea venture MoU and skilled-migration frameworks were signed.|Customs and other sector cooperation also featured.','An MoU, investment decision, operating factory and actual worker placement are different milestones.','Strategic autonomy requires evaluating interests and constraints across partnerships.|Do not treat a migration framework as unrestricted employment or signed cooperation as completed production.','A bilateral summit does not prove all announced projects were implemented immediately.','How can long-standing partnerships adapt to changing economic and strategic conditions?')
add('International Relations','02 · Oman CEPA','Oman CEPA signed: tariff lines versus trade value','The countries signed the comprehensive agreement.','Oman offers zero-duty access on over 98% of tariff lines.|India’s concessions concern about 78% of lines, covering nearly 95% of import value.|Services and investment also feature.','A tariff line is a product classification; its count is not the same as its share of actual trade value.','Benefits depend on entry into force, schedules, origin rules and non-tariff conditions.|AP goods/services exporters must examine their own products rather than rely on aggregate percentages.','Do not equate 78% of lines with 78% of import value or signature with immediate universal duty-free trade.','What determines effective use of a bilateral trade agreement?',True)
add('International Relations','03 · New Zealand negotiations','India–NZ conclusion: correct date and coverage denominator','The primary announcement is dated 22 December, not the PRS reference’s 18 December.','Negotiations concluded; this is distinct from entry into force.|India offered liberalisation in 70% of tariff lines covering about 95% of bilateral trade coverage stated in the announcement.|The announced USD 20 billion investment facilitation spans fifteen years.','Conclusion, signature, ratification/commencement and realised trade are separate stages.','The primary release’s tariff-line share corrects the review’s imprecise 95% export phrasing.|A 5,000-at-any-time professional pathway is not unlimited guaranteed migration or 5,000 automatic annual jobs.','Do not call the investment already received or all Indian sensitive products opened without exceptions.','How should trade-negotiation outcomes be assessed beyond headline market-access claims?',src=['E7-NZ','E7-PRS12'],day=22)
add('Society & Welfare','06 · Labour-rule consultation','December Labour Code drafts: the next implementation stage','The government invited comments on central draft rules.','The OSH draft specifies a forty-eight-hour working week.|Wage calculations and floor-wage consultation have procedural detail.|Industrial-relations drafts address unions, standing orders and notices.','Code commencement in November does not make every December draft clause final.','Compare parent-law protections with the mechanisms needed for enforcement.|Final central/state rules and applicability must be checked for the relevant establishment.','Do not describe a draft as nationwide operative detail or assume all daily hours were finalised uniformly.','Why do labour reforms depend on rule design and enforcement after commencement?',True)
add('Society & Welfare','07 · Platform social protection','Gig-worker eligibility: draft thresholds versus paid benefits','Social-security draft rules propose eligibility conditions.','The draft refers to ninety days with one aggregator.|For multiple aggregators it refers to 120 days in the last financial year.|Additional centrally specified conditions may apply.','Meeting a draft engagement threshold differs from enrolment in a functioning benefit scheme.','Portability needs credible platform records, accessible corrections and financing.|Do not infer all gig workers already had PF/insurance paid from statutory recognition alone.','The 90/120-day proposals are not proof of universal automatic benefits already delivered in December.','How can platform-worker protection handle fragmented work histories?',True)
add('Society & Welfare','08 · Skilling audit','PMKVY audit: certification is not verified placement','CAG examined three phases launched between 2015 and 2022.','The review reports 23 lakh placements out of 56 lakh certified in specified short-term/special-project components.|Skill-gap planning and convergence were weak.|Documentation and monitoring gaps were identified.','The denominator excludes some components; a placement ratio does not necessarily establish sustained employment or adequate pay.','Align training with district demand and verify retention, wages and employer feedback.|Do not label this a current placement rate for every phase or every trained person.','The reported 41% is component- and audit-period-specific, not an all-time unemployment rate.','How should public skilling programmes be judged beyond certificates?',True)
add('Economy','09 · Coal allocation','CoalSETU: end-use flexibility with exclusions','A new non-regulated-sector linkage window was introduced.','Linkages may last up to fifteen years.|Traders are excluded; coking coal is not offered.|Existing specified end-use auctions continue alongside it.','A coal linkage is a supply arrangement, not an unrestricted mining lease or universal trading licence.','Flexible use needs transparent allocation and monitoring.|Keep notified policy separate from the month’s MMDR and coal-exchange drafts.','Do not extend the window to traders/coking coal or describe all coal regulation as abolished.','How can resource allocation improve flexibility without losing accountability?',p='P2')
add('Polity & Governance','03 · Digital constitutionalism','Digital power: consent and proportionality beyond an app','The magazine discusses the subsequently withdrawn pre-installation mandate.','Its case context is Sanchar Saathi pre-installation, later withdrawn.|The framework applies liberty, equality, privacy and accountability to digital power.|State authority and platform power pose different legal questions.','The existence of a service does not prove every installation is mandatory, and withdrawal must be reflected in chronology.','Evaluate lawful purpose, necessity, alternatives and independent redress.|Do not conflate withdrawal of mandatory installation with abolition of the service itself.','A withdrawn mandate is not an ongoing compulsory-installation rule.','How should constitutional safeguards apply to digital public infrastructure?',slug='digital-constitutionalism')
add('Polity & Governance','04 · PESA and community authority','PESA: Fifth Schedule modifications and legal harmonisation','The December issue revisits the 1996 Act.','PESA extends Part IX with modifications to Fifth Schedule Areas.|It recognises customary/community governance and Gram Sabha roles.|Consultation, recommendation and consent requirements need the exact provision.','Fifth Schedule PESA and Sixth Schedule autonomous councils are not interchangeable.','AP application needs state rules, actual devolution and alignment with land/mineral/forest law.|1996 to December 2025 is twenty-nine completed years; avoid a loose completed-thirty-years claim.','Do not apply PESA uniformly to all AP territory or replace every consultation duty with an identical absolute veto.','What makes tribal self-governance effective beyond formal statutory recognition?',True,slug='panchayats-extension-to-scheduled-areas-act-1996')
add('Society & Welfare','09 · Workplace redress','PoSH: the woman’s workplace committee and outsider harassment','The issue reports the Sohail Malik judgment’s jurisdictional clarification.','A complaint may be handled by the committee at the aggrieved woman’s workplace even when the respondent works elsewhere.|Workplace protection includes more than only physical contact.|Confidentiality and fair inquiry are separate safeguards.','Jurisdiction to inquire is not automatic proof of guilt or a waiver of the respondent’s due process.','Institutional access must work with coordination, confidentiality and effective remedy.|The primary judgment was not independently read in this pass; use it for precise operative limits.','Do not assume outsider harassment automatically falls outside all workplace committee jurisdiction.','How can workplace redress remain accessible, confidential and procedurally fair?',True,slug='prevention-of-sexual-harassment-posh-act-2013')
add('Environment','03 · Groundwater denominator','Groundwater 2025: national averages hide local stress','The issue reviews CGWB/state assessment data.','Annual recharge is reported as 448.52 BCM.|Extractable resources are 407.75 BCM and extraction 247.22 BCM.|The stage of extraction is 60.63%.','Stage of extraction uses annual extraction divided by annual extractable resources, not total recharge.','A national average below 100% does not establish every block is safe or water is uncontaminated.|AP mandal-level assessment and crop/water-quality evidence should guide local action.','Do not use total recharge as the ratio denominator or treat all assessed aquifers as equally sustainable.','How should groundwater policy integrate quantity, quality and local demand?',True,slug='dynamic-groundwater-resources-assessment')
add('Environment','04 · Community risk reduction','Local DRR: integrate risk into Gram Panchayat planning','A community-based project was approved in the magazine account.','The outlay is ₹507.37 crore.|MoPR and NDMA jointly implement the project.|The described coverage is twenty states and eighty-one disaster-prone districts.','Community participation must include risk identification, planning and evaluation, not volunteer response alone.','Link GPDP budgets, accessible warnings and local vulnerability mapping.|A national project announcement does not establish every AP panchayat is funded or trained.','Do not call planned model panchayats already disaster-proof or coverage universal.','How can local government make disaster-risk reduction part of routine development?',True,slug='localization-of-disaster-risk-reduction-drr')
add('Society & Welfare','10 · Digital work boundaries','Right to disconnect: proposal versus enforceable protection','The issue discusses a private member’s Bill and comparative laws.','The objective is protection from routine work contact outside working hours.|Essential/on-call duties need clearly defined arrangements.|The Indian proposal is not automatically enacted law.','Rest, dignity and unequal bargaining power inform the analysis; comparative law is not domestic entitlement.','Specify emergencies, compensation and remedies rather than a blanket operational impossibility.|Do not use a single reported death as proof of a clinically established cause.','A private member’s introduction does not create an immediately universal legal right.','How can work-boundary protection accommodate essential services without normalising constant availability?',slug='right-to-disconnect',p='P2')
add('Society & Welfare','11 · Children and social platforms','Australia’s under-sixteen rule: a comparative case, not Indian law','The December issue reviews the enforced Australian age restriction.','Covered platforms must take steps to prevent underage accounts.|Age-assurance design raises privacy and exclusion questions.|India’s child-data and online-safety rules are separate instruments.','A country’s platform age limit differs from a universal ban on all internet use by children.','Evaluate safety outcomes, evasion, data minimisation and access to support.|Do not infer causation for every mental-health outcome from correlation with social-media use.','Do not call the Australian rule an Indian under-sixteen ban or a ban on all online services.','What makes child-online-safety policy effective and rights-respecting?',slug='social-media-ban-for-children',p='P2')
add('Culture & History','01 · Living heritage','Deepavali: intangible heritage, not a World Heritage monument','UNESCO’s official profile records the 2025 inscription.','It is on the Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity.|The practice is transmitted through families and communities.|It involves diverse rituals, skills and social participation.','The 2003 living-heritage framework differs from the 1972 World Heritage sites convention.','Safeguarding supports communities and evolving practice rather than freezing one authorised form.|Recognition is not an exemption from health, safety or environmental rules.','Do not describe the inscription as a newly designated physical World Heritage site or ownership monopoly.','How can living heritage be safeguarded while allowing community-led adaptation?',src=['E7-ICH'],slug='unesco-intangible-cultural-heritage-list',p='P2')
add('Andhra Pradesh','01 · Administrative geography','AP district reorganisation: two additions, total twenty-eight','The newspaper reports final notifications effective 31 December.','Markapuram and Polavaram are the two new districts.|Polavaram headquarters is Rampachodavaram; Markapuram headquarters is Markapuram.|Madanapalle becomes Annamayya headquarters, not an automatically separate third addition.','A headquarters shift, new revenue division and new district are different administrative actions.','Distinguish November proposals from the final December account.|Official gazette boundary schedules remain the authority for any mandal-specific exam or service question.','Do not repeat the earlier three-new-districts/29-total proposal as the final arrangement.','How should district reorganisation be judged by access and administrative capacity?',True,src=['E7-DIST'],day=31)
add('Andhra Pradesh','02 · Rayalaseema development requests','Rayalaseema horticulture package: request, not sanctioned grant','The CM sought Central support in December.','The reported request is a ₹41,000 crore horticulture-development package.|The proposal links clusters, processing and regional development.|Support for the Polavaram–Nallamala Sagar link was also sought.','A memorandum, budget allocation, project appraisal, clearance and completed irrigation are separate stages.','For Kadapa/Rayalaseema, examine water reliability, markets, cold chains and farmer risk.|Do not turn requested funding or proposed diversion volumes into sanctioned spending or final interstate entitlement.','A request to the Union Finance Minister is not proof the package was approved or all project clearances obtained.','What complements public investment in a resilient horticulture strategy for Rayalaseema?',True,src=['E7-HORT'])
